To compare the performance of URM with other skyline reducing algorithms on the DOT dataset, we have implemented and tested several skyline reducing algoriths: K-Means REEDY (KRSP), EIQUE [31], N AIVE GREEDY [32], /epsilon1-ADR greedy (/epsilon1-ADR) [33], and S KYCOVER [34]. 

The regret ratio of the output from our URM algorithm is consistently lower than that of other algorithms. This demonstrates how effective our algorithm can be in finding a representative set with small regret ratios even when initialized with suboptimal starting points, as shown in Figs. 12 and 14.

The results for the DOT dataset with dimensions 4 and  cups are presented in Fig. 12 and Fig. 14. We denote KRSPG REEDY as RSP, NAIVE GREEDY as NG, EIQUE as EQ, /epsilon1-ADR greedy as /epsilon1-ADR and SKYCOVER as SC in the plots. The orange bars show the regret ratio of the output from our (URM) algorithm when initialized with the corresponding skyline reducing algorithms' outputs. As expected URM outperforms other algorithms.
